    feat(node): reap caches, job dirs and stale clones before disk-floor refusal — a node below its floor refused admission without reclaiming anything, so a full host could never recover. Addresses CF-007 (AC3).
    
    scripts/reclaim_disk.py reaps only fixed user-space targets under the node's own $HOME
    (.cache/pip, .cache/uv, .cache/pre-commit, .cache/go-build, .npm/_cacache, plus
    .node/jobs and .node/clones entries older than the TTL). It refuses `/` and any root
    whose real path does not contain the target, never follows a symlink, and never touches
    repo/, .node/node.json, .node/crier.json or .node/floor.toml.
    
    project-node.sh layer 00 now runs that reclaim before refusing, re-measures free space,
    reports the freed MiB and refuses only if still below the floor. --check stays read-only
    (CF-025 purity): it prints the existing disk FAIL row plus what --apply would reap.
    node-create.sh stages the new script so it reaches a node; specs/NODE.md gains the
    reclaim rule and N-5 carries the ordering.
    
    Evidence: python3 -B tests/test_reclaim.py -> 9 tests OK; python3 -B tests/test_disk_floor.py
    -> 12 tests OK; bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS (section 20 proves ordering, check
    purity, fail-closed missing reclaimer and idempotence); scripts/boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK.
    AC5 (bunker residue reaping) stays open: it needs an authorized live host.
    
